    <briefdescription>
<para>Nonempty view. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Head</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="structlibbirch_1_1Range" kindref="compound">Range</ref> or <ref refid="structlibbirch_1_1Index" kindref="compound">Index</ref> type. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Tail</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>View type.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
A view describes the active elements over <computeroutput>D</computeroutput> dimensions of an array. It consists of a <emphasis>head</emphasis> range or index for the first dimension, and a <emphasis>tail</emphasis> view for the remaining <computeroutput>D - 1</computeroutput> dimensions, recursively. The tail view is <ref refid="structlibbirch_1_1EmptyView" kindref="compound">EmptyView</ref> for the last dimension. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
